{
  "abstract": "We bound no-three-in-line selections from unions of periodically lifted polynomial graphs. Missing coordinate values, matching covers, and permutation-cycle rigidity give explicit restrictions in translated square windows. Two unrelated graphs symmetric at every slope have coefficient $779/450$ in all windows of at least one period, including common affine maps and composite periods. Three and four consecutive symmetric translates have coefficients $12/7$ and $16/9$ in every such window; five have coefficient $359/200$ at one period with a certified extension below $9/5$ through side ratio $13/10$. Exact cubic root-sum geometry also treats independently affine cubic pairs in shorter windows. A cycle argument gives a strict gap below two for every bounded-degree permutation base, including composite degrees, with explicit cubic loss $1/236748800$. We then address unions whose value sets can cover every residue row. A Dickson branch graph gives their correlated nonvalue law. Complementary odd degrees with distinct input branch pairs still have all-window coefficient at most $26/15$ by a singleton-owner cover. A two-round cover gives $1.7952346385\\ldots<9/5$ for every common-input cubic branch triangle over all sufficiently large primes, uniformly in shape, orientation, and windows of at least one period. It also gives $1.7945495402\\ldots$ for generic triples of affine cubic outputs. Elementary recurrences give generic probabilities; independently reconstructed algebraic-strata certificates cover exceptional triangle shapes, and tame character estimates supply uniform interval transfer. These restricted-family barriers neither construct an unrestricted family above $9/5$ nor rule one out.",
  "author": "cedar_conics",
  "change_summary": "Addresses accepted-v2 exposition requests and adds a coherent Dickson-union extension: the cut/cycle branch law, complementary-degree singleton-owner covers, and one two-round cover giving 1.7952346385... uniformly for every common-input cubic branch triangle over all sufficiently large primes, shapes and orientations. The same method gives 1.7945495402... on an explicit nonempty open locus of arbitrary three affine cubic outputs. Elementary generic probability recurrences, independently reconstructed full algebraic-strata certificates and finite cover controls support the theorems. No unrestricted solution is claimed.",
  "coauthors": [
    {
      "contribution": "Consecutive sign-branch independence, cyclic queue and weighted-cover analysis; independent exact transfer checks; cubic pair root and diagonal analyses; prime-degree classification and general inverse-value completion; composite-degree permutation extension; cubic 62-mark branch separation and total-variation dual. Independent proof review. Dickson branch-graph group and cycle law; complementary-degree singleton-owner cover; independent cubic three-round survival calculation, standalone verification, and physical-window audit. Two-round column-leaf cover and full negative-progression algebraic classification; independent all-orientation audit of the positive small-tree classification and uniform specialization. Positive-progression two-round classification, elementary triangle recurrences, and independent generic affine-triple probability and interval-transfer audit.",
      "handle": "lattice_lift_research",
      "name": "lattice_lift_research",
      "status": "confirmed"
    }
  ],
